---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";

const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<SiteLayout
  title="AI providers"
  description="The provider architecture and current integration status for Veasel Code."
>
  <section class="doc-page page-grid">
    <p class="kicker">FIELD GUIDE / PROVIDERS</p>
    <h1>
      Bring the model
      <br />
      <em>you want to work with.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Veasel Code keeps model connections behind a small V provider interface.
      Choose from 35 presets across three wire protocols and use the same
      persistent session workflow. Presets are not 35 independent native SDK
      integrations: most hosted and local choices use the shared
      OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions adapter.
    </p>
    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Available in the current source build</h2>
      <p>
        The V backend streams bounded responses, keeps credentials server-side,
        and stores each successful user/assistant exchange in the session
        database. Provider-native tool calls can request bounded, workspace
        listing, file reads, literal search, and a single-file edit proposal. A
        proposal is a saved diff; it does not modify the workspace until a
        person opens and approves it in the TUI. Requested file content and tool
        results go back to the configured provider. Model responses stream
        through durable session events. A model can also propose a shell
        command; the TUI requires opening the exact command, working directory,
        and timeout before approval. Approved commands run as the server user
        without an OS sandbox. Shell output and requested file content are
        returned to the configured provider.
      </p>
      <div
        class="provider-table"
        role="table"
        aria-label="Provider implementation status"
      >
        <div class="provider-table-row provider-table-head" role="row">
          <b role="columnheader">Provider</b>
          <b role="columnheader">Status</b>
          <b role="columnheader">Notes</b>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">OpenAI-compatible</b>
          <span role="cell">Available</span>
          <span role="cell">
            Default adapter; custom HTTPS or loopback endpoint
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">Anthropic</b>
          <span role="cell">Available</span>
          <span role="cell">Native Messages API</span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">Gemini</b>
          <span role="cell">Available</span>
          <span role="cell">Native generateContent API</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Provider presets</h2>
      <p>
        Anthropic and Gemini use their native HTTP APIs. The remaining presets
        use OpenAI Chat Completions; provider-specific authentication and
        features are not implied. Choose an entry in Settings with <kbd>s</kbd>
        on the home screen or <code>/models</code> in a session.
      </p>
      <h3>Hosted and gateway endpoints</h3>
      <p>
        <a href="https://doc-en.302.ai/5030894m0">302.AI</a>,
        <a href="https://help.aliyun.com/en/model-studio/compatibility-of-openai-with-dashscope">
          Alibaba Cloud Model Studio,
        </a>
        Cerebras, Cloudflare Workers AI, DeepInfra, DeepSeek, Fireworks AI,
        <a href="https://www.gmicloud.ai/en/developers">GMI Cloud</a>, Groq,
        Hugging Face, Hyperbolic, Mistral, Moonshot AI, Nebius AI Studio, Novita
        AI, NVIDIA NIM, OpenAI, OpenAI-compatible custom endpoints, OpenRouter,
        Perplexity, SambaNova, SiliconFlow, Together AI, Vercel AI Gateway,
        Venice AI, xAI, and <a href="https://docs.z.ai/">Z.AI</a>.
      </p>
      <h3>Local endpoints</h3>
      <p>
        <a href="https://opencode.ai/docs/providers/">Atomic Chat</a>, Ollama,
        llama.cpp, LM Studio, LocalAI, and vLLM. They start with loopback URLs
        and do not require an API key by default. Change the endpoint when your
        local server uses another address. Cloudflare Workers AI needs its
        account ID in the endpoint URL. Alibaba Cloud Model Studio defaults to
        its US Virginia endpoint; select the URL that matches your account's
        region and API key.
      </p>
      <h3>Model selection</h3>
      <p>
        When a saved profile or environment variable already supplies provider
        credentials, Settings can fetch that endpoint's model list. This is a
        model-list request, not a generation request. If credentials are not
        configured yet, the endpoint does not support listing, or the request
        fails, enter a model ID manually. The selected provider, model,
        endpoint, and key can all be configured from Settings; API keys are
        never returned by the settings API. See the{" "}
        <a href={`${basePath}/docs/api/`}>model-list endpoint</a> for its
        contract.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Choose a provider in Veasel</h2>
      <p>
        Press <kbd>s</kbd> on the home screen or enter <code>/models</code> in
        an open session. Enter the provider ID, model ID, API base URL, and key.
        Veasel keeps a separate profile for each provider. Leave the key blank
        to keep the saved value, or enter <code>!clear</code> to remove it. Keys
        are never shown again in the TUI or returned by the API.
      </p>
      <p>
        Profiles live in <code>$VEASEL_DATA_DIR/model-settings.json</code>; on
        POSIX, the file is restricted to the current user. Values are stored in
        plaintext on disk, so use environment variables when local policy
        requires secrets to be managed by an OS keychain.
      </p>
      <h3>Headless configuration</h3>
      <pre><code>export VEASEL_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic
export VEASEL_MODEL=your-model-name
export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-api-key
v run . serve</code></pre>
      <p>
        Use <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code> with
        <code>openai-compatible</code>, or <code>GEMINI_API_KEY</code> with
        <code>gemini</code>. Set <code>VEASEL_MODEL_BASE_URL</code> for a
        compatible endpoint; custom endpoints require HTTPS or loopback HTTP.
        Environment configuration remains available for scripts and automation.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="callout">
      <strong>Today:</strong> configured sessions can stream responses, inspect
      the selected workspace through bounded tools, propose a single-file edit
      for review, and restore recent history. Applying a proposal requires
      opening its diff and explicitly approving it in the TUI. Proposed shell
      commands require the same exact review and approval before running, but
      have no OS sandbox. File excerpts and tool output are sent to your
      configured provider. See the
      <a href="https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/blob/main/docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md">
        implementation plan
      </a>
      for current progress.
    </p>
    <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/architecture/`}>
      See the architecture <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    </a>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
